  "prefLabel": "Gen 305 ELIGIBILITY FOR PROVISIONAL LICENSURE",
  "recordType": "rule-part",
  "ruleText": "PART Gen 305 ELIGIBILITY FOR PROVISIONAL LICENSURE\n\n(a) Gen 305.01 Eligibility Requirements for Provisional Licensure. Eligibility requirements for provisional licensure shall be:\n\n(a) An academic degree which is at least a master’s degree;\n\n(b) Authorization to take the certification exam required in Gen 303.03(a);\n\n(c) Good professional character and reliability as evidenced by:\n\n(1) The answers to the questions from the application form specified in Plc 304.03 and Plc 304.04; and\n\n(2) The criminal offender record report(s) required by RSA 328-F:18-a.\n\nSource. #10686, eff 10-7-14; ss by #13555, eff 4-11-23; ss by #14337, eff 10-7-25, EXPIRES: 10-7-35\n\nPART 306 PRACTICE UNDER A PROVISIONAL LICENSE",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/gen300.html"
